From f931071560265d69f75ffa5f2ccfaebb75e8758c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shyalya <shyalya@turtle-server.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:21:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Fix playerbot battlegrounds: queueing, combat, and
 flag-carrier behaviour
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Queueing (bots never actually got into battlegrounds at all):
- Bots queuing for a BG now go through the opcode handler directly instead of ai->QueuePacket() — bot sessions are never registered in sWorld.m_sessions, so World::UpdateSessions() never drained their recvQueue and the join packet silently vanished forever.
- Falls back to a server-accepted dummy battlemaster guid (1337) when no physical Battlemaster NPC is loaded nearby, instead of requiring one.
- WSG/AB matches get a 20-minute hard cutoff (winner = whoever leads on points/flags) so bot-heavy matches that never cap objectives don't run forever.

Combat (bots only ever fought back when a human directly attacked them — never proactively, never assisting each other). Three independent causes:
- The +pvp strategy's "enemy player near" trigger was only registered for the combat engine, which an idle bot never entered on its own. Now also registered for the non-combat engine and applied to both on BG entry.
- The underlying "enemy player targets" list was built exclusively from "attackers" — units already in an active threat relationship — so an idle enemy who hadn't attacked anyone was invisible to the whole detection chain. Now falls back to "possible targets" (a real proximity scan, no threat-table dependency) while in a battleground.
- AttackEnemyFlagCarrierAction::isUseful() tested the wrong unit's aura (copy-pasted from a neighbouring function), requiring the *attacking* bot to already carry a flag itself instead of checking the *target*. Bots chased flag carriers forever without ever attacking once they caught up.

Flag carriers:
- No longer freeze forever mid-map when the enemy also holds our flag. They previously got sent to a random "hiding spot" in that case, and a separate safety guard then permanently refused to pick a new objective once the bot arrived. They now head straight for base — worst case waiting there until our flag returns.
- Bots no longer walk to the enemy flag spawn on their own initiative (they patrol instead); they still defend their own carrier and chase whoever holds our flag. Exception: if the bot's own team has zero real players, it resumes actively fetching — checked per team, not "anyone in the match", since a solo human always counts as present on their own team. A human playing solo against an all-bot team therefore still faces opposition that tries to cap, while matches with real players on both sides are unaffected.
